  "notes": "USAGE:\nAlso used as a suru verb: {結束|けっそく}する (to unite, to band together). Carries a positive nuance of strength through togetherness, often used in contexts of overcoming adversity.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {結束|けっそく}が{固|かた}い: tight-knit solidarity\n- {結束|けっそく}を{強|つよ}める: to strengthen unity\n- {結束|けっそく}を{高|たか}める: to heighten cohesion\n- {結束|けっそく}{力|りょく}: power of unity\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{団結|だんけつ} (solidarity) is very close in meaning but has a stronger political or organizational nuance, often used for unions and protest movements. {結束|けっそく} is more general.",
